  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle.\n• Half-fill a medium saucepan with boiling water.\n• Cook egg noodles over medium-high heat, stirring occasionally with a fork to separate, until tender, 4-5 minutes.\n• Drain, rinse and set aside.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f87b5ecade9b9f0acf61ba/step-13678400.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, roughly chop Asian greens.\n• Cut Japanese tofu into 2cm chunks.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f87b5ecade9b9f0acf61ba/step-0a6d4710.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat a generous drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.\n• When oil is hot, cook tofu, turning occasionally, until golden, 3-4 minutes. Transfer to a bowl.\n• Return frying pan to a medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook broccoli florets, tossing, until tender, 5-6 minutes.\n• Add Asian greens and stir-fry until slightly wilted, 1 minute.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f87b5ecade9b9f0acf61ba/step-8abc6e20.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Reduce heat to medium, then stir in Japanese curry paste, coconut milk, soy sauce mix and the water and cook until combined, 1-2 minutes.\n• Stir through cooked egg noodles and baby spinach leaves until wilted and combined. Season with salt and pepper to taste.\n• Divide egg noodles and coconut curry broth between bowls. Top with Japanese tofu.\n• Tear over coriander and sprinkle over crispy shallots to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67f87b5ecade9b9f0acf61ba/step-11dbbe30.jpg"
    }
  ]
